From: ProjectM TV contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Clamp local built-in wave RGB before nonzero brightening

Follow original MilkDrop2 ordered float RGB comparisons. Modify local
submission color only; preserve raw frame variables, alpha, geometry,
Native styles, primitive counts, replay and every darken predicate.
No pass, target or draw is added by this arithmetic block.

--- a/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/Waveform.cpp
+++ b/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/Waveform.cpp
@@ -321,3 +321,12 @@
-
+
-    if (*presetPerFrameContext.wave_brighten > 0)
+    // Original MilkDrop clamps float RGB before optional normalization.
+    // Comparisons preserve authored NaN instead of inventing a replacement.
+    if (waveR < 0) waveR = 0;
+    if (waveG < 0) waveG = 0;
+    if (waveB < 0) waveB = 0;
+    if (waveR > 1) waveR = 1;
+    if (waveG > 1) waveG = 1;
+    if (waveB > 1) waveB = 1;
+
+    if (*presetPerFrameContext.wave_brighten != 0)
     {
